# {{.ProjectName}}

This is a Go project generated using gobuild CLI tool (fiber preset).

It ships a [Fiber v3](https://github.com/gofiber/fiber) HTTP server with a
`/health` endpoint and graceful shutdown.

## Prerequisites

- Go {{.GoVersion}} or higher
- Make (optional, for using Makefile commands)

## Installation

1. Clone this repository:
   ```bash
   git clone <your-repo-url>
   cd {{.ProjectName}}
   ```

2. Install dependencies:
   ```bash
   go mod tidy
   ```

## Usage

### Using Make commands

- Run the project:
  ```bash
  make run
  ```

### Direct Go commands

- Run the project:
  ```bash
  go run main.go
  ```

The server listens on `APP_PORT` (default `8080`). Once running, check the
health endpoint:

```bash
curl http://localhost:8080/health
# {"status":"ok"}
```

Send `Ctrl+C` (SIGINT) to trigger a graceful shutdown.

## Project Structure

- `main.go`: Fiber app bootstrap, route mounting, graceful shutdown
- `internal/handler/health.go`: `/health` handler
- `go.mod`: Go module definition
- `go.sum`: Go module checksums
- `.env`: Environment variables
- `Makefile`: Build and development commands
- `README.md`: Project documentation

